@page "/products"

<PageTitle>Practice 2: Products</PageTitle>

<h1>Practice 2: Service-to-Result&lt;T&gt; Refactor</h1>

<div class="alert alert-success">
    <strong>Complete!</strong> ProductService now returns <code>Result&lt;Product&gt;</code>
    instead of throwing exceptions. ProductEffects checks <code>result.IsSuccess</code>
    instead of using try/catch.
</div>

<div class="card mt-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h5>Refactored Methods</h5>
        <ul>
            <li><code>GetByIdAsync</code> -- returns <code>Result&lt;Product&gt;</code> with validation and not-found errors</li>
            <li><code>AddAsync</code> -- accumulates name and price errors before returning</li>
            <li><code>UpdateAsync</code> -- returns <code>Result&lt;Product&gt;</code> with all validation paths</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>
